questions.question:
Given below are two statements :
<b>Statement I</b>:
\text{D-(+)-glucose} + \text{D-(+) fructose} \xrightarrow{-H_{2}O} \text{sucrose}
\text{sucrose} \xrightarrow{\text{Hydrolysis}} \text{D-(+)-glucose} + \text{D-(+) fructose}
<b>Statement II</b> : Invert sugar is formed during sucrose hydrolysis.
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below -

questions.explanation:
The monosaccharide units obtained from hydrolysis of oligosaccharides may be or may not be same. For example:
\text{Lactose} \xrightarrow{\text{H}_{3}\text{O}^{\oplus}} \text{Glucose} + \text{Galactose}
different monosaccharide units
\text{Maltose} \xrightarrow{\text{H}_{3}\text{O}^{\oplus}} \text{Glucose} + \text{Glucose}
same monosaccharide units

questions.question:
A linear octasaccharide (molar mass = 1024 g \(mol^{-1}\)) on complete hydrolysis produces three monosaccharides: ribose, 2-deoxyribose and glucose. The amount of 2-deoxyribose formed is 58.26% (w/w) of the total amount of the monosaccharides produced in the hydrolyzed products. The number of ribose unit(s) present in one molecule of octasaccharide is \(\underline{\hspace{1cm}}\) .
Use : Molar mass (in g \(mol^{-1}\)): ribose = 150, 2-deoxyribose = 134, glucose = 180;
Atomic mass (in amu): H = 1, O = 16
